  <item>
    <title>Hayman Burn Area</title>
    <link>https://hobobiker-prep.ddev.site/hayman_burn_area</link>
    <description>&lt;p&gt;We rode through the incredible Hayman Fire burn area (from the 2002 fire seasn) on the second day out. People told us it was like World War III, but we found it quite different. There was lots of ground cover, lots of green. The black trees were quite stark, but it was really a pleasant day. But the Goose Creek road we took had us gaining more than 4000 feet of elevation, and it was rough! What a day1&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
